  "worked_solution": "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\overset{\u2015}{[\\begin{aligned}7-8\\text{i} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{7-8\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{\u2015}{6}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7+8\\text{i} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
